<title>USA: Public Service Electric &amp; Gas sells $235 mln bonds.</title>
<headline>Public Service Electric &amp; Gas sells $235 mln bonds.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-06-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following issue of first and refunding mortgage bonds from Public Service Electric and Gas Company was priced on Thursday.</p>
<p>The offering was done via a competitive won by Morgan Stanley Dean Witter, according to the company.</p>
<p>BORROWER PUBLIC SERVICE ELECTRIC AND GAS COMPANY</p>
<p>AMT $235 MLN	 COUPON 6.50 PCT    MATURITY 6/1/2000</p>
<p>TYPE BONDS	   ISS PRICE 100.00   FIRST PAY DATE 12/1/1997</p>
<p>LAST MOODY'S A3    YIELD 6.50 PCT     PAY FREQ  SEMI-ANNUAL</p>
<p>S&amp;P A-MINUS				   CALLABLE  NO</p>
<p>U.S. Corporate Bond Unit, 212-859-1678</p>
</text>
